# Little Physics documentation

This repo (`LittlePhysicsDocs`) documents the Unity package **Little Physics** (`com.ivancodes.littlephysics`).

## Reference sources (read before writing)

Use these files in `.cursor/files/` plus the package code. **Do not edit the reference files from this repo** — they are author notes; published docs live under `docs/`.

### Documentation text source

**When writing or expanding documentation prose, read `.cursor/files/Little Physics Documentation - doc.txt` first.** That file is the authoritative draft for user-facing text: product pitch, features, limitations, quick start, pipeline narrative, body types, LOD, spatial map, singleton data structures, custom job groups, builders, and related explanations. Expand and adapt its content into published pages under `docs/` — do not invent parallel wording when `doc.txt` already covers the topic.

| File | Role |
|------|------|
| `.cursor/files/Little Physics Documentation - doc.txt` | **Main prose source** — read this for documentation text (see above) |
| `.cursor/files/Little Physics Documentation - pipeline.pdf` | **Pipeline diagram** — system-group hierarchy, update order, which groups are public vs internal |
| `.cursor/files/Little Physics Documentation - public.txt` | **Public API index** — exhaustive list of types to document (authorings, components, job interfaces, builders, enums, editor tools) |

Package path (implementation source of truth for names, defaults, and behavior):

`C:\Work\LittlePhysicsSystem\Packages\com.ivancodes.littlephysics`

### Source priority when they disagree

1. **Package `.cs` files** — field names, defaults, API signatures, system group names
2. **`pipeline.pdf`** — execution order and group nesting
3. **`.cursor/files/Little Physics Documentation - doc.txt`** — user-facing explanations and feature descriptions
4. **`.cursor/files/Little Physics Documentation - public.txt`** — coverage checklist (ensure every listed public type gets a doc page or section)

Example: `doc.txt` / `public.txt` say `LittlePhysicsUserImportGroup` — code and `pipeline.pdf` use `LittlePhysicsImportGroup`. Document the **code name**.

## Product facts (from reference sources)

- **Display name:** Little Physics
- **Unity:** 6000.0+ (Unity 6). Not compatible with Unity 2022.
- **Entities:** `com.unity.entities` 1.4.8
- **Namespace:** `LittlePhysics`
- **Scale:** up to ~1,000,000 units (spheres-only dynamic bodies, LOD, Burst, multithreading)
- **Trade-off:** loose settings reduce determinism — suited for crowds, particles, liquids
- **Time scale:** `0` (pause), `1`, `2`, `4` only (`LittlePhysicsTimeComponent`)
- **Substeps:** 1–4 per fixed update (`PhysicsSettingsAuthoring`)
- **Samples:** Package Manager → Little Physics → **All Samples** (5 scenes; requires Entities.Graphics)

### Features to highlight

Deep simulation tuning, LOD (up to 4 levels), pause/slow/fast, dynamic/static/kinematic/triggers, directional + radial gravity, friction, surface collisions (every dynamic body vs surfaces each frame), substeps.

### Known limitations (document honestly)

- Determinism drops with loose LOD/settings; closer camera ranges improve it
- `MaxEntitiesCount` cap — excess entities ignored
- **Dynamic bodies: spheres only**; kinematic/static: spheres + capsules; surfaces: spheres, capsules, simple plane, box, reverse sphere
- Object-to-object collisions only inside the **Spatial Map** bounds; outside map still gets gravity + surface collision
- Time scale limited to 0, 1, 2, 4

