## Page front matter

Every doc page needs:

```yaml
---
title: Human-readable title
layout: default
nav_order: 2          # omit on child pages; use parent instead
parent: API Reference # required for API child pages
description: One sentence for search and SEO
tags: [authoring, physics, dynamic-body]  # optional; indexed by search
---
```

Use `has_children: true` and `permalink:` only on section index pages (see `docs/api-reference/index.md`).

### Unique titles (required)

Just the Docs builds the sidebar by matching `parent` to another page’s `title`. **All titles site-wide must be unique**, especially parent section titles. Duplicate titles (e.g. Guides and API both using `Builders` or `PhysicsBodyData`) break child navigation.

- **API Reference** pages: keep exact C# type names (`DynamicBodyBuilder`, `IBodiesJob`, …).
- **Guides** that cover the same types: use distinct titles (`Using builders`, `Using IBodiesJob`, `PhysicsBodyData overview`, …).
- `parent:` must match the parent page’s `title` exactly.

## File naming

Convert C# type names to kebab-case filenames:

| C# type | Doc file |
