### Image file structure

**Image folders must mirror the doc page path under `docs/`.** Drop the `docs/` prefix; use a folder per page; put one or more image files inside that folder.

| Doc page | Image folder |
|----------|--------------|
| `docs/guides/builders/dynamic-body-builder/index.md` | `assets/images/guides/builders/dynamic-body-builder/` |
| `docs/api-reference/dynamic-body-authoring.md` | `assets/images/api-reference/dynamic-body-authoring/` |
| `docs/getting-started/index.md` | `assets/images/getting-started/` |

- For `index.md` pages, the image folder matches the page’s directory (not `index/`).
- For single `.md` files, the image folder matches the filename without `.md`.
- Use descriptive image filenames inside the folder (e.g. `inspector.png`, `diagram.png`), not a flat `{page-name}-inspector.png` at the root of `assets/images/`.

Example:

```
assets/images/guides/builders/dynamic-body-builder/inspector.png
```

Markdown reference:

```markdown
![Dynamic Body Builder inspector]({{ site.baseurl }}/assets/images/guides/builders/dynamic-body-builder/inspector.png)
```

## Writing rules

- Use exact type names from code (`DynamicBodyAuthoring`, not "Rigidbody Component")
- Pull feature/limitation prose from `.cursor/files/Little Physics Documentation - doc.txt`; verify against code before publishing
- Document subscene + baking workflow — ECS, not classic MonoBehaviour physics
- Note co-dependencies (`PhysicsVelocityAuthoring` only on dynamic bodies)
- Note warnings from source (velocity ignored on `SurfaceBodyAuthoring`)
- For custom jobs: prefer package job interfaces; use `SimulationDataComponent` physics JobHandle for import/export scheduling
- Replace `_config.yml` / `index.md` placeholders when publishing
- Expand reference material from `.cursor/files/Little Physics Documentation - doc.txt` — do not paste it verbatim into published pages

